924
00:42:02,851 --> 00:42:06,320
Remember, I asked if you weren't making rice cakes?

925
00:42:06,321 --> 00:42:07,361
It almost killed me.

926
00:42:08,061 --> 00:42:09,590
I heard things break next door.

927
00:42:09,591 --> 00:42:12,661
No wonder our kitchen shook and all.

928
00:42:14,501 --> 00:42:15,561
- It was me.
- I see.

929
00:42:16,031 --> 00:42:18,030
- Give me one of each.
- Is it dried seaweed?

930
00:42:18,031 --> 00:42:19,900
- Dried seaweed?
- One each, please.

931
00:42:19,901 --> 00:42:21,271
Push it in.

932
00:42:21,401 --> 00:42:23,011
Give me a second.

933
00:42:23,711 --> 00:42:25,211
Fatsia shoot fritter is good.

934
00:42:25,981 --> 00:42:27,501
- What's good?
- Fatsia shoot fritter.

935
00:42:28,611 --> 00:42:29,851
(Crunchy)

936
00:42:30,081 --> 00:42:32,111
The fatsia shoots are super crunchy.

937
00:42:32,651 --> 00:42:33,751
It's crunchy.

938
00:42:35,351 --> 00:42:37,521
(And next to the rice dough balls)

939
00:42:37,551 --> 00:42:39,190
Fatsia shoots and squash.

940
00:42:39,191 --> 00:42:41,191
(Fatsia shoots and kabocha squash fritters)

941
00:42:41,391 --> 00:42:42,491
Fatsia shoots.

942
00:42:43,891 --> 00:42:46,131
This ingredient could be the highlight.

943
00:42:46,461 --> 00:42:49,300
- Fatsia shoots.
- Fatsia shoots. These are big ones.

944
00:42:49,301 --> 00:42:51,731
(Fatsia shoots)

945
00:42:51,831 --> 00:42:53,500
It was deep-fried to keep the aroma.

946
00:42:53,501 --> 00:42:55,501
(Fatsia shoot fritters with the scent of spring)

947
00:42:55,571 --> 00:42:56,641
It smells much stronger.

948
00:42:59,081 --> 00:43:00,340
The fatsia shoots are great.

949
00:43:00,341 --> 00:43:02,451
Give me some fatsia shoots. I want to deep-fry some.

950
00:43:04,981 --> 00:43:07,750
Thank you. Thank you very much.

951
00:43:07,751 --> 00:43:08,821
What a relief.

952
00:43:11,051 --> 00:43:12,151
What's this?

953
00:43:13,091 --> 00:43:15,520
It's risotto and seafood.

954
00:43:15,521 --> 00:43:16,737
(Spring Vegetables Risotto by Shin Ga Young)

955
00:43:16,761 --> 00:43:17,891
It's ours.

956
00:43:18,691 --> 00:43:21,101
Risotto is much like porridge, so I'm sure they'll enjoy it.

957
00:43:21,361 --> 00:43:22,471
This one is good too.

958
00:43:23,971 --> 00:43:26,271
This one is delicious. It is.

959
00:43:30,641 --> 00:43:32,801
- It's not mustard, so what is it?
- It's not mustard.

960
00:43:33,181 --> 00:43:34,310
Is it beans?

961
00:43:34,311 --> 00:43:36,280
(Spring vegetables salsa verde: Sauce made from extracted juices)

962
00:43:36,281 --> 00:43:38,311
Here. Try it.

963
00:43:40,751 --> 00:43:41,981
I like how it's not salty.

964
00:43:42,551 --> 00:43:43,590
Is it delicious?

965
00:43:43,591 --> 00:43:45,550
The finishing touches were...

966
00:43:45,551 --> 00:43:46,620
It's too salty.

967
00:43:46,621 --> 00:43:47,721
- Salty?
- Yes.

968
00:43:48,021 --> 00:43:49,930
We try to make it bland,

969
00:43:49,931 --> 00:43:51,807
but the elders always ask us to make it more bland.

970
00:43:51,831 --> 00:43:54,701
You're right. We should make it bland.

971
00:43:55,061 --> 00:43:56,901
It's this one. The aromatic spring vegetables.

972
00:43:57,771 --> 00:43:59,141
Risotto and seafood.

973
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:01,401
That's risotto and seafood.

974
00:44:02,241 --> 00:44:04,341
It felt like they recognised that effort.

975
00:44:05,211 --> 00:44:07,081
Didn't we have many risotto dishes?

976
00:44:07,241 --> 00:44:08,711
It looked like we had several.

977
00:44:09,011 --> 00:44:10,411
- This is another risotto.
- Yes.

978
00:44:10,511 --> 00:44:12,181
All the rice dishes are risotto.

979
00:44:12,521 --> 00:44:16,151
(Kim Hee Eun made a different kind of risotto.)

980
00:44:16,321 --> 00:44:17,897
- The dish was no joke.
- I know, right?

981
00:44:17,921 --> 00:44:19,590
- With a grand topping.
- What was no joke about it?

982
00:44:19,591 --> 00:44:20,691
It's just tteokgalbi.

983
00:44:21,061 --> 00:44:23,331
- No, it wasn't just tteokgalbi.
- No.

984
00:44:23,831 --> 00:44:26,901
(Shrimp, shiitake mushroom, fatsia shoots)

985
00:44:27,261 --> 00:44:31,001
I think one of the customers just scooped some of our risotto.

986
00:44:32,641 --> 00:44:35,101
This is like porridge, isn't it?

987
00:44:36,841 --> 00:44:39,541
I told them it was Italian-style porridge,

988
00:44:39,811 --> 00:44:41,131
in case they didn't know risotto.

989
00:44:41,741 --> 00:44:44,511
- Risotto? It's risotto.
- Yes.

990
00:44:45,181 --> 00:44:47,220
It's something a lot like tteokgalbi.

991
00:44:47,221 --> 00:44:48,621
She said it was tteokgalbi.

992
00:44:50,121 --> 00:44:51,291
- It's good.
- Hold on.

993
00:44:52,421 --> 00:44:53,490
Is it good?

994
00:44:53,491 --> 00:44:54,691
- It's very soft.
- It's good.

995
00:44:55,761 --> 00:44:57,661
I'm a fan of this one.

996
00:44:57,731 --> 00:44:59,500
- Which one?
- The risotto.

997
00:44:59,501 --> 00:45:00,501
(Kim Hee Eun's risotto gets good reviews.)

998
00:45:00,502 --> 00:45:01,600
The one with tteokgalbi?

999
00:45:01,601 --> 00:45:05,101
I heard it was something with porridge and dried seaweed.

1000
00:45:07,201 --> 00:45:10,271
Imagine how happy the old ladies must be to be served food...

1001
00:45:10,511 --> 00:45:13,041
after cooking for others every single day.

1002
00:45:14,241 --> 00:45:15,280
Eating food made by someone else is...

1003
00:45:15,281 --> 00:45:16,611
- amazing.
- Totally.

1004
00:45:16,781 --> 00:45:19,151
Little did I think such a day would come.

1005
00:45:19,821 --> 00:45:21,920
(Laughing)

1006
00:45:21,921 --> 00:45:22,991
Really.

1007
00:45:23,651 --> 00:45:26,191
Tell them to host this every year.

1008
00:45:26,791 --> 00:45:27,921
Every year, okay?

1009
00:45:29,891 --> 00:45:31,361
- It's all rice, right?
- Yes.

1010
00:45:32,091 --> 00:45:33,131
This one is...

1011
00:45:34,361 --> 00:45:36,871
Provence-style vegetable pot rice.

1012
00:45:38,301 --> 00:45:40,170
It's totally different from risotto, right?

1013
00:45:40,171 --> 00:45:42,741
- The texture of the rice.
- It's the complete opposite.

1014
00:45:43,241 --> 00:45:45,671
I wonder if the customers will like the texture.

1015
00:45:47,011 --> 00:45:48,440
What if they say, "It's not thoroughly cooked?"

1016
00:45:48,441 --> 00:45:51,781
But it seemed like the rice was fully cooked.

1017
00:45:51,981 --> 00:45:54,720
- It's like something we always had.
- We're used to it.

1018
00:45:54,721 --> 00:45:56,251
This one tastes much like pizza.

1019
00:45:56,651 --> 00:45:58,351
- Pizza.
- I like it.

1020
00:45:58,651 --> 00:46:00,191
- It's French.
- Something like that.

1021
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:02,361
Like Korean steamed rice.

1022
00:46:03,091 --> 00:46:04,451
- I'm full.
- I prefer mushy rice.

1023
00:46:06,231 --> 00:46:09,330
(The lady next to her also tries a spoonful.)

1024
00:46:09,331 --> 00:46:10,500
- So?
- You've got to chew for a while.

1025
00:46:10,501 --> 00:46:12,871
(Shaking her head)

1026
00:46:15,476 --> 00:46:18,615
(The lady next to her also tries a spoonful.)

1027
00:46:18,616 --> 00:46:19,685
- So?
- You've got to chew for a while.

1028
00:46:19,686 --> 00:46:22,016
(Shaking her head)

1029
00:46:24,116 --> 00:46:26,285
The rice in this one is... You know...

1030
00:46:26,286 --> 00:46:28,956
- It's not sticky rice.
- The rice is fluffy.

1031
00:46:29,326 --> 00:46:31,556
It reminds me of fried rice.

1032
00:46:31,956 --> 00:46:35,026
This Odae Rice tastes like a different type of rice.

1033
00:46:35,426 --> 00:46:37,026
- How come?
- It's like Vietnamese rice.

1034
00:46:37,266 --> 00:46:39,386
- It was roasted. That's why.
- The rice was roasted.

1035
00:46:39,936 --> 00:46:42,306
The rice is all fluffy and nice.

1036
00:46:44,106 --> 00:46:48,976
(Did the old ladies like the French-style pot rice?)

1037
00:46:50,016 --> 00:46:52,015
Trying something new is really enjoyable.

1038
00:46:52,016 --> 00:46:53,086
Totally.

1039
00:46:53,286 --> 00:46:55,715
- We're having luxurious food today.
- Really.

1040
00:46:55,716 --> 00:46:57,436
- Where else would we have this?
- Exactly.

1041
00:46:58,286 --> 00:46:59,655
What was this one again?

1042
00:46:59,656 --> 00:47:00,886
Jeongabok.

1043
00:47:01,526 --> 00:47:03,156
- It has abalone inside.
- Right.

1044
00:47:03,556 --> 00:47:05,426
- It's a high-end dish.
- Let's try it.

1045
00:47:06,166 --> 00:47:07,802
When will we ever get to eat something like this?

1046
00:47:07,826 --> 00:47:08,995
It'd cost a fortune...

1047
00:47:08,996 --> 00:47:10,916
- Think of the price.
- if we had it at a hotel.

1048
00:47:11,296 --> 00:47:13,136
Have an abalone each.

1049
00:47:13,236 --> 00:47:14,806
Abalone is a pricey dish.

1050
00:47:15,866 --> 00:47:17,635
Who used abalone?

1051
00:47:17,636 --> 00:47:19,276
Over here. Jeongabok.

1052
00:47:19,406 --> 00:47:21,176
- Jeongabok.
- Three delicacies.

1053
00:47:21,546 --> 00:47:22,676
It's an expensive dish.

1054
00:47:23,246 --> 00:47:26,646
I don't think they'll write down five dollars for it.

1055
00:47:27,446 --> 00:47:30,486
I was hoping my dish would look expensive.

1056
00:47:30,756 --> 00:47:34,386
If the old ladies were to put a price on each dish,

1057
00:47:34,986 --> 00:47:37,395
I thought it'd be best to make a dish...

1058
00:47:37,396 --> 00:47:39,366
that would command a higher price.

1059
00:47:40,466 --> 00:47:43,396
- Jeongabok is a great idea.
- For real.

1060
00:47:43,936 --> 00:47:45,595
If you made a dish look more pricey with the same money for ingredients,

1061
00:47:45,596 --> 00:47:47,076
- that's a skill of yours.
- Totally.

1062
00:47:48,306 --> 00:47:49,405
This one's amazing.

1063
00:47:49,406 --> 00:47:50,575
(Yuxiang shiitake mushrooms by Kim Ho Yoon)

1064
00:47:50,576 --> 00:47:51,705
How's this one?

1065
00:47:51,706 --> 00:47:54,945
(Yuxiang shiitake mushrooms by Kim Ho Yoon)

1066
00:47:54,946 --> 00:47:56,116
She asked how it was.

1067
00:47:56,276 --> 00:47:57,675
- It's good.
- I'm savouring it right now.

1068
00:47:57,676 --> 00:47:58,745
- Try it.
- Okay.

1069
00:47:58,746 --> 00:48:00,616
(Yuxiang shiitake mushrooms by Kim Ho Yoon)

1070
00:48:00,886 --> 00:48:02,015
It's rice inside.

1071
00:48:02,016 --> 00:48:04,185
The mushroom was grilled until golden...

1072
00:48:04,186 --> 00:48:06,256
- with rice inside.
- There's shrimp inside.

1073
00:48:06,356 --> 00:48:07,825
Yes, there's seafood.

1074
00:48:07,826 --> 00:48:09,855
- Seafood. Shrimp.
- The mushroom is the best part.

1075
00:48:09,856 --> 00:48:12,395
The rice has been grilled until golden at the end.

1076
00:48:12,396 --> 00:48:13,665
- This one?
- Yes.

1077
00:48:13,666 --> 00:48:15,325
- The outside?
- Like nurungji.

1078
00:48:15,326 --> 00:48:16,466
- Yes.
- Try it.

1079
00:48:16,696 --> 00:48:18,735
How did they stuff the filling?

1080
00:48:18,736 --> 00:48:20,106
Right? Cooking it... Gosh.

1081
00:48:20,706 --> 00:48:23,075
What's the name of this dish again? It's good.

1082
00:48:23,076 --> 00:48:24,475
- Raw shiitake mushroom...
- Shrimp paste.

1083
00:48:24,476 --> 00:48:25,635
- shrimp paste.
- Shrimp paste?

1084
00:48:25,636 --> 00:48:27,306
- I like that one better.
- Me too.

1085
00:48:28,006 --> 00:48:29,946
This shiitake mushroom is great.

1086
00:48:30,976 --> 00:48:31,976
Is it?

1087
00:48:31,977 --> 00:48:33,716
- Yes.
- It's good.

1088
00:48:35,286 --> 00:48:36,656
I wonder how it will turn out.

1089
00:48:37,956 --> 00:48:39,056
The reaction...

1090
00:48:39,956 --> 00:48:41,276
Every dish will get a full score.

1091
00:48:41,756 --> 00:48:43,226
All of them are good.

1092
00:48:44,326 --> 00:48:46,672
It's good. Try the shiitake mushroom. There's only one left.

1093
00:48:46,696 --> 00:48:47,726
Have it.

1094
00:48:48,326 --> 00:48:51,066
(Glancing)

1095
00:48:51,436 --> 00:48:53,466
- What did you cook?
- Seven side dishes.

1096
00:48:54,906 --> 00:48:56,676
- Seven?
- Amazing.

1097
00:48:57,036 --> 00:48:58,876
It's all or nothing.

1098
00:48:59,206 --> 00:49:02,345
The others made main dishes.

1099
00:49:02,346 --> 00:49:03,446
(The only side dish)

1100
00:49:03,776 --> 00:49:07,246
As I had expected, there were many risottos.

1101
00:49:08,986 --> 00:49:12,886
I thought the customers would need something refreshing at one point.

1102
00:49:15,456 --> 00:49:16,596
The outside?

1103
00:49:17,156 --> 00:49:18,796
- My stomach feels unsettled.
- Suddenly?

1104
00:49:19,566 --> 00:49:20,766
Everything is...

1105
00:49:21,726 --> 00:49:22,866
a bit cheesy.

1106
00:49:23,266 --> 00:49:24,536
It was good at first.

1107
00:49:25,436 --> 00:49:26,836
- I want kimchi.
- Same here.

1108
00:49:27,566 --> 00:49:29,166
There aren't many refreshing dishes.

1109
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:31,806
All were heavy.

1110
00:49:33,646 --> 00:49:35,566
We should've added some Cheongyang chilli pepper.

1111
00:49:36,446 --> 00:49:37,846
These must be side dishes for rice.

1112
00:49:37,976 --> 00:49:39,846
She said they were side dishes.

1113
00:49:40,086 --> 00:49:42,045
The side dishes look good with the rice.

1114
00:49:42,046 --> 00:49:43,256
Totally.

1115
00:49:43,486 --> 00:49:45,955
It's called Spring Picnic Feast.

1116
00:49:45,956 --> 00:49:47,402
(Spring Picnic Feast by Jo Seo Hyung)

1117
00:49:47,426 --> 00:49:48,686
It's good.

1118
00:49:49,026 --> 00:49:50,396
The tomato kimchi is great.

1119
00:49:50,726 --> 00:49:52,195
Try the tomato kimchi.

1120
00:49:52,196 --> 00:49:53,566
The tomato kimchi is the best.

1121
00:49:54,096 --> 00:49:55,565
The cheonhyehyang inside...

1122
00:49:55,566 --> 00:49:57,565
Right? It takes away...

1123
00:49:57,566 --> 00:49:59,135
that oiliness.

1124
00:49:59,136 --> 00:50:00,735
Yes, the tanginess...

1125
00:50:00,736 --> 00:50:02,806
- This one?
- balances out the richness.

1126
00:50:03,106 --> 00:50:04,406
I like the side dishes.

1127
00:50:05,276 --> 00:50:08,776
If they considered the side dishes as one cuisine,

1128
00:50:08,906 --> 00:50:10,676
we might have a chance of surviving.

1129
00:50:11,616 --> 00:50:13,845
If we were to rank them 1st, 2nd, and 3rd...

1130
00:50:13,846 --> 00:50:14,916
Among these?

1131
00:50:15,116 --> 00:50:16,255
This comes in first place for me.

1132
00:50:16,256 --> 00:50:17,886
- Oh, my. Really?
- All were good, no?

1133
00:50:18,086 --> 00:50:19,256
I choose this one.

1134
00:50:20,186 --> 00:50:21,856
- This was the best.
- First place.

1135
00:50:22,086 --> 00:50:24,956
I can't decide as everything was just too good.

1136
00:50:25,656 --> 00:50:27,196
True. I'm wavering.

1137
00:50:27,666 --> 00:50:28,896
At first...

1138
00:50:29,196 --> 00:50:32,496
I was happy to see them enjoying the dishes.

1139
00:50:32,906 --> 00:50:34,306
But when the time to evaluate came,

1140
00:50:34,866 --> 00:50:35,966
they all turned...

1141
00:50:36,606 --> 00:50:38,206
cool-headed and sharp.

1142
00:50:39,206 --> 00:50:40,606
I put my soul into it.

1143
00:50:40,906 --> 00:50:42,576
I want to advance.

1144
00:50:42,776 --> 00:50:44,816
What if we have to close our store soon?

1145
00:50:46,146 --> 00:50:48,016
If it's 2 teams out of the 8 teams...

1146
00:50:50,416 --> 00:50:52,585
Thanks to them, I had a delicious meal.

1147
00:50:52,586 --> 00:50:55,856
(The 100 guests are done dining.)

1148
00:50:56,356 --> 00:50:58,155
- Voting.
- We have to vote.

1149
00:50:58,156 --> 00:51:00,226
We have to leave after voting in that booth.

1150
00:51:01,766 --> 00:51:03,995
- What about this one?
- I'm going with this one.

1151
00:51:03,996 --> 00:51:06,235
(Voting with 1 10-dollar bill and 10 1-dollar bills)

1152
00:51:06,236 --> 00:51:07,265
This one.

1153
00:51:07,266 --> 00:51:08,465
That was good too.

1154
00:51:08,466 --> 00:51:10,305
(They can use 20 dollars for 1 dish or multiple dishes.)

1155
00:51:10,306 --> 00:51:11,435
Do I put it in here?

1156
00:51:11,436 --> 00:51:13,305
- I choose this one.
- This dish was the best.

1157
00:51:13,306 --> 00:51:14,676
I enjoyed this one.

1158
00:51:15,546 --> 00:51:16,546
All done.

1159
00:51:16,547 --> 00:51:18,576
(The 100 guests are done voting.)

1160
00:51:19,376 --> 00:51:22,186
The revival match has ended.

1161
00:51:25,116 --> 00:51:26,385
I'm getting nervous again.

1162
00:51:26,386 --> 00:51:28,786
(Street Arena)

1163
00:51:30,956 --> 00:51:32,296
Really, this is cruel.

1164
00:51:33,526 --> 00:51:34,766
Luck must be on our side.

1165
00:51:35,726 --> 00:51:37,196
Is your fortune good this year?

1166
00:51:38,596 --> 00:51:40,476
I don't think so based on how well we're doing.

1167
00:51:42,306 --> 00:51:43,736
The jeongabok was...

1168
00:51:44,406 --> 00:51:45,436
Is that so?

1169
00:51:46,406 --> 00:51:48,906
Should we have just made tteokgalbi and no risotto?

1170
00:51:52,616 --> 00:51:54,892
I'm getting flashbacks of how hard spicy stir-fried pork was.

1171
00:51:54,916 --> 00:51:56,116
The cauldron soft tofu.

1172
00:51:57,216 --> 00:51:58,486
This is stressing me out.

1173
00:51:59,926 --> 00:52:00,986
The results...

1174
00:52:01,526 --> 00:52:04,526
of the revival match will be announced.

1175
00:52:12,196 --> 00:52:13,466
Out of the eight teams,

1176
00:52:13,866 --> 00:52:16,836
only the two with the highest revenue...

1177
00:52:17,676 --> 00:52:19,876
will revive and advance to Round Three.

1178
00:52:20,906 --> 00:52:22,645
(Become rich, Number One)

1179
00:52:22,646 --> 00:52:23,716
The possibility...

1180
00:52:24,076 --> 00:52:25,446
wasn't dead low.

1181
00:52:26,386 --> 00:52:27,546
Won't I make it...

1182
00:52:28,586 --> 00:52:29,816
in the top two?

1183
00:52:30,816 --> 00:52:33,226
I was fully confident about our dish.

1184
00:52:33,626 --> 00:52:36,896
We won't lose. We won't be overpowered. That was all I thought.

1185
00:52:37,296 --> 00:52:38,756
We're on the brink.

1186
00:52:39,326 --> 00:52:40,626
We must survive.

1187
00:52:43,496 --> 00:52:44,596
Here is...

1188
00:52:44,936 --> 00:52:47,936
the lowest revenue of the revival match.

1189
00:52:50,206 --> 00:52:51,475
- I don't want to hear it.
- This is cruel.

1190
00:52:51,476 --> 00:52:52,506
Right?

1191
00:52:53,006 --> 00:52:54,286
Are we starting from the bottom?

1192
00:52:54,746 --> 00:52:55,846
I'm nervous.

1193
00:52:56,476 --> 00:52:57,716
Unbelievable.

1194
00:52:58,016 --> 00:52:59,245
Our revenue might be the lowest.

1195
00:52:59,246 --> 00:53:01,146
Our dish was creamy.

1196
00:53:02,846 --> 00:53:04,756
The final revenue of the eighth place.

1197
00:53:05,456 --> 00:53:07,186
One hundred and thirty-two dollars.

1198
00:53:07,426 --> 00:53:08,456
What?

1199
00:53:08,856 --> 00:53:10,225
- That's mean.
- Among 100 guests?

1200
00:53:10,226 --> 00:53:11,226
Yes.

1201
00:53:11,356 --> 00:53:13,156
If I were given 10-dollar and 1-dollar bills,

1202
00:53:13,196 --> 00:53:15,266
that 10-dollar bill would be my 1st choice.

1203
00:53:15,526 --> 00:53:16,865
If I don't get that ten-dollar bill,

1204
00:53:16,866 --> 00:53:18,906
it'd be meaningless regardless of how well I do it.

1205
00:53:20,006 --> 00:53:21,766
- Right away?
- Please.

1206
00:53:21,966 --> 00:53:23,776
Please let us survive.

1207
00:53:30,316 --> 00:53:31,845
(Number One, Everything About Tteokbokki, )

1208
00:53:31,846 --> 00:53:33,315
(The Star In My Heart, Bol A Bol, Don't Tell Grandma, )

1209
00:53:33,316 --> 00:53:34,845
(Extraordinary Couple, Wolfie's, Essence And Technique)

1210
00:53:34,846 --> 00:53:37,356
(The Star In My Heart)

1211
00:53:37,586 --> 00:53:39,086
The Star In My Heart...

1212
00:53:39,656 --> 00:53:42,996
had the lowest revenue and failed to revive.

1213
00:53:43,156 --> 00:53:44,226
- What?
- What?

1214
00:53:44,426 --> 00:53:45,996
The Star In My Heart.

1215
00:53:46,096 --> 00:53:47,125
My goodness.

1216
00:53:47,126 --> 00:53:48,595
- I thought it was us.
- I thought it was us.

1217
00:53:48,596 --> 00:53:50,196
The Star In My Heart.

1218
00:53:51,636 --> 00:53:54,206
- It sounded like "Extraordinary."
- I thought it was us.

1219
00:53:54,436 --> 00:53:56,335
I guess that was because they served side dishes.

1220
00:53:56,336 --> 00:53:57,575
They did a lot of things.

1221
00:53:57,576 --> 00:53:58,736
I know.

1222
00:53:58,906 --> 00:54:00,946
Was ours worth only 132 dollars?

1223
00:54:01,646 --> 00:54:03,176
I don't think it was that bad.

1224
00:54:04,646 --> 00:54:07,246
It couldn't beat the main dishes.

1225
00:54:09,246 --> 00:54:11,686
The side dishes are not so popular.

1226
00:54:11,786 --> 00:54:12,885
These ones?

1227
00:54:12,886 --> 00:54:14,625
We have so many fancy dishes here.

1228
00:54:14,626 --> 00:54:15,726
It tastes good, though.

1229
00:54:16,356 --> 00:54:18,895
We're busy eating other dishes. Since these are side dishes,

1230
00:54:18,896 --> 00:54:20,295
we're not eating them yet.

1231
00:54:20,296 --> 00:54:22,395
Actually, when I saw...

1232
00:54:22,396 --> 00:54:24,436
the ladies holding one-dollar bills,

1233
00:54:24,866 --> 00:54:27,836
I realised we picked the wrong menu item.

1234
00:54:28,336 --> 00:54:31,406
Side dishes are what people never want to spend a lot of money on.

1235
00:54:31,836 --> 00:54:33,445
Because we're used...

1236
00:54:33,446 --> 00:54:36,546
to side dishes served for free at a restaurant,

1237
00:54:36,876 --> 00:54:39,176
people don't view them as proper dishes on their own.

1238
00:54:41,146 --> 00:54:44,316
I completely failed to read their minds.

1239
00:54:47,186 --> 00:54:49,026
You never know how things will turn out.

1240
00:54:51,296 --> 00:54:53,366
The final revenue of the seventh place...

1241
00:54:53,696 --> 00:54:55,666
is 163 dollars.

1242
00:54:55,826 --> 00:54:57,166
It's really low.

1243
00:55:09,306 --> 00:55:12,415
Bol A Bol has failed to survive.

1244
00:55:12,416 --> 00:55:13,856
(7th place: Lim Ki Hak and Kim Hoon)

1245
00:55:14,086 --> 00:55:15,886
To be honest, the sales numbers...

1246
00:55:16,046 --> 00:55:17,816
are a bit disappointing.

1247
00:55:18,556 --> 00:55:21,486
This Odae Rice tastes like a different type of rice.

1248
00:55:21,626 --> 00:55:23,426
- How come?
- It's like Vietnamese rice.

1249
00:55:24,056 --> 00:55:25,156
The rice is a little...

1250
00:55:25,896 --> 00:55:27,966
It has a Western flavour to it.

1251
00:55:28,996 --> 00:55:29,996
(They found the French-style pot rice too unfamiliar.)

1252
00:55:29,997 --> 00:55:31,517
The rice grains are too light and dry.

1253
00:55:33,136 --> 00:55:35,336
The final revenue of the sixth place...

1254
00:55:36,036 --> 00:55:37,806
is 175 dollars.

1255
00:55:38,076 --> 00:55:39,136
It's so tight.

1256
00:55:39,636 --> 00:55:42,376
The gap is less than ten dollars.

1257
00:55:43,006 --> 00:55:44,976
- There's barely any difference.
- You're right.

1258
00:55:46,016 --> 00:55:47,286
Number One...

1259
00:55:47,716 --> 00:55:49,485
has failed to survive.

1260
00:55:49,486 --> 00:55:50,685
(6th place: Kwak Dong Hoon and Song Ji Beom)

1261
00:55:50,686 --> 00:55:52,285
It’s too salty, so I don't like it.

1262
00:55:52,286 --> 00:55:53,455
What's too salty?

1263
00:55:53,456 --> 00:55:54,686
Only this one is too salty.

1264
00:55:54,886 --> 00:55:56,286
It's a bit on the salty side.

1265
00:55:56,756 --> 00:55:58,655
The seasoning styles of Busan and Gangwon Province...

1266
00:55:58,656 --> 00:55:59,726
are totally different.

1267
00:56:01,026 --> 00:56:02,866
Ours was seasoned the Busan way.

1268
00:56:03,136 --> 00:56:05,236
The final revenue of the fifth place...

1269
00:56:05,866 --> 00:56:07,806
is 184 dollars.

1270
00:56:09,736 --> 00:56:11,006
Wolfie's...

1271
00:56:11,336 --> 00:56:13,305
has failed to survive.

1272
00:56:13,306 --> 00:56:16,376
(5th place: Lee Jae Hoon and Kim Jin Gyo)

1273
00:56:16,516 --> 00:56:18,875
The scores are so close, and they're being so strict.

1274
00:56:18,876 --> 00:56:20,686
I bet one team is totally dominating.

1275
00:56:21,746 --> 00:56:24,785
(The sales status of the revival match)

1276
00:56:24,786 --> 00:56:28,986
(Only the 1st and 2nd places will survive.)

1277
00:56:29,326 --> 00:56:30,626
My gosh, this is...

1278
00:56:30,956 --> 00:56:32,226
Then, it's us and...

1279
00:56:32,556 --> 00:56:34,026
Them and Essence And Technique.

1280
00:56:34,726 --> 00:56:36,666
The remaining restaurants are...

1281
00:56:36,996 --> 00:56:39,936
Essence And Technique, Extraordinary Couple,

1282
00:56:40,606 --> 00:56:41,936
Don't Tell Grandma,

1283
00:56:42,336 --> 00:56:44,306
and Everything About Tteokbokki.

1284
00:56:46,076 --> 00:56:47,545
- Please.
- Out of these four,

1285
00:56:47,546 --> 00:56:51,076
we will now reveal the two restaurants to survive.

1286
00:56:53,616 --> 00:56:56,286
- Please.
- Please. Just this once...

1287
00:56:57,316 --> 00:56:58,555
(A hearty meal with Korean beef tteokgalbi)

1288
00:56:58,556 --> 00:57:00,355
We wanted to give the feeling...

1289
00:57:00,356 --> 00:57:02,025
of having enjoyed a proper, satisfying meal...

1290
00:57:02,026 --> 00:57:03,626
while also eating healthy.

1291
00:57:04,856 --> 00:57:06,226
- Hong Geun.
- Yes?

1292
00:57:07,526 --> 00:57:08,566
We can do this.

1293
00:57:09,166 --> 00:57:11,535
We used spring vegetables and greens...

1294
00:57:11,536 --> 00:57:13,765
to make it fresh and light,

1295
00:57:13,766 --> 00:57:15,366
so we were sure they'd love it.

1296
00:57:16,036 --> 00:57:17,205
This makes me hold out hope.

1297
00:57:17,206 --> 00:57:18,976
Gosh, no. This is too hard.

1298
00:57:20,446 --> 00:57:23,445
I was hoping the customers would focus on...

1299
00:57:23,446 --> 00:57:25,715
how Cheorwon rice was used.

1300
00:57:25,716 --> 00:57:27,676
(Perilla seed cream rice dough ball and fritters)

1301
00:57:30,316 --> 00:57:32,485
It’s light but packed with aroma...

1302
00:57:32,486 --> 00:57:33,825
and flavour.

1303
00:57:33,826 --> 00:57:36,456
(Yuxiang shiitake mushrooms with Odae rice)

1304
00:57:36,486 --> 00:57:38,995
The two restaurants that will be revived are...

1305
00:57:38,996 --> 00:57:40,966
Please.

1306
00:57:56,202 --> 00:57:57,401
- Essence And Technique.
- It's Essence And Technique.

1307
00:57:57,402 --> 00:57:59,201
- Everything About Tteokbokki.
- What?

1308
00:57:59,202 --> 00:58:00,202
They have been revived.

1309
00:58:02,342 --> 00:58:07,711
(Kim Ho Yoon and Jung Chan Hee have survived.)

1310
00:58:07,712 --> 00:58:08,882
I didn't see this coming.

1311
00:58:09,282 --> 00:58:10,282
- Congratulations.
- What?

1312
00:58:10,283 --> 00:58:12,111
(Kim Kwan Hoon and Shin Jong Hun have survived.)

1313
00:58:12,112 --> 00:58:13,211
- Congratulations.
- Second place,

1314
00:58:13,212 --> 00:58:14,332
Everything About Tteokbokki.

1315
00:58:14,922 --> 00:58:17,852
- Good job.
- The final revenue is 377 dollars.

1316
00:58:18,452 --> 00:58:19,898
The first place, Essence And Technique.

1317
00:58:19,922 --> 00:58:22,522
The final revenue is 529 dollars.

1318
00:58:23,122 --> 00:58:26,791
The two restaurants have survived in the revival match.

1319
00:58:26,792 --> 00:58:27,832
Great job.

1320
00:58:28,902 --> 00:58:29,962
Don't cry.

1321
00:58:30,972 --> 00:58:32,132
Why are you crying?

1322
00:58:34,842 --> 00:58:38,172
I thought about the customers from the 2nd half of Round 2.

1323
00:58:39,472 --> 00:58:40,672
"Let's do it right this time."

1324
00:58:41,182 --> 00:58:42,982
"Let's make it even more delicious for them."

1325
00:58:43,512 --> 00:58:44,712
Taste this one more time.

1326
00:58:46,252 --> 00:58:47,558
What if we make it a bit sweeter?

1327
00:58:47,582 --> 00:58:48,682
It's a little spicy.

1328
00:58:48,852 --> 00:58:50,221
We need to tone it down and make it smoother.

1329
00:58:50,222 --> 00:58:52,182
The sesame oil aroma isn't really coming through.

1330
00:58:53,192 --> 00:58:55,722
I wanted to stay completely focused...

1331
00:58:56,122 --> 00:58:57,731
and make sure the same mistake will never happen again.

1332
00:58:57,732 --> 00:59:00,262
All I could think was to make the food taste better.

1333
00:59:00,632 --> 00:59:02,562
I like the mushroom dish the best.

1334
00:59:02,862 --> 00:59:04,602
I'll grab another shiitake mushroom.

1335
00:59:04,972 --> 00:59:06,212
The shiitake mushroom is great.

1336
00:59:06,472 --> 00:59:07,601
You guys like the mushroom dish, right?

1337
00:59:07,602 --> 00:59:09,522
I think the mushroom dish will take first place.

1338
00:59:10,442 --> 00:59:12,572
- Okay.
- This was definitely the best.

1339
00:59:13,372 --> 00:59:16,181
(132 dollars, 163 dollars, 175 dollars, 184 dollars)

1340
00:59:16,182 --> 00:59:17,352
The mushroom.

1341
00:59:17,652 --> 00:59:18,712
It was great.

1342
00:59:18,952 --> 00:59:21,622
- I liked this one best.
- Only this one.

1343
00:59:22,352 --> 00:59:25,851
We took up a quarter of the total budget,

1344
00:59:25,852 --> 00:59:28,392
so mathematically speaking, that's a very high rate.

1345
00:59:28,892 --> 00:59:31,432
We learn so much from every single round.

1346
00:59:31,862 --> 00:59:35,032
I'm so happy that I'm given one more chance like this.

1347
00:59:36,562 --> 00:59:39,302
I think we should change our name to Everything About Drama.

1348
00:59:39,602 --> 00:59:41,272
Everything we do is quite dramatic.

1349
00:59:42,002 --> 00:59:43,071
(Round 1)

1350
00:59:43,072 --> 00:59:45,411
Everything About Tteokbokki. Congratulations.

1351
00:59:45,412 --> 00:59:49,542
(They survived in 18th place out of 20 teams.)

1352
00:59:49,982 --> 00:59:53,621
(They fought neck and neck against Lee Yeon Bok, the master chef.)

1353
00:59:53,622 --> 00:59:55,651
(But they suffered a heartbreaking defeat.)

1354
00:59:55,652 --> 00:59:58,851
We always dropped to rock bottom,

1355
00:59:58,852 --> 01:00:00,961
but we grabbed a lifeline to climb back up again and again.

1356
01:00:00,962 --> 01:00:02,362
That’s what happened this time too.

1357
01:00:02,492 --> 01:00:05,462
For me, the rice dough ball is number one.

1358
01:00:05,792 --> 01:00:07,901
- The rice dough ball.
- I like it.

1359
01:00:07,902 --> 01:00:09,702
- It's nice.
- I like the cream sauce.

1360
01:00:12,532 --> 01:00:15,272
I'm so grateful to the ladies who enjoyed our dish.

1361
01:00:15,572 --> 01:00:18,072
When I looked at their plates, there were no leftovers.

1362
01:00:19,512 --> 01:00:21,412
It made the joy of victory twice as sweet.

1363
01:00:23,652 --> 01:00:26,182
The six eliminated restaurants...

1364
01:00:26,282 --> 01:00:28,782
will leave the Street Arena.

1365
01:00:29,052 --> 01:00:32,121
I've been running restaurants for 12 years now,

1366
01:00:32,122 --> 01:00:33,921
but I don't think I've ever told myself...

1367
01:00:33,922 --> 01:00:36,392
things like, "Good job. You worked hard."

1368
01:00:36,622 --> 01:00:38,491
So today, before I leave,

1369
01:00:38,492 --> 01:00:41,102
I want to say it to myself just this once.

1370
01:00:41,702 --> 01:00:43,771
Good job. You worked hard too.

1371
01:00:43,772 --> 01:00:45,272
- Good job.
- Good job.

1372
01:00:45,802 --> 01:00:48,802
Running a business is a truly lonely fight.

1373
01:00:49,202 --> 01:00:52,372
I've been through so much over those 12 years.

1374
01:00:55,342 --> 01:00:58,212
Even though I got eliminated, I want to tell myself...

1375
01:00:58,682 --> 01:01:00,212
that I did well.

1376
01:01:00,752 --> 01:01:04,091
I believe that my business is the driving force...

1377
01:01:04,092 --> 01:01:05,752
that changed my life.

1378
01:01:06,022 --> 01:01:08,422
Good restaurants with delicious food always make a comeback.

1379
01:01:09,422 --> 01:01:11,062
If someone gets revived,

1380
01:01:11,262 --> 01:01:14,132
that means someone else has to pack their bags and go home.

1381
01:01:15,062 --> 01:01:17,272
It might have been a little unconventional,

1382
01:01:17,802 --> 01:01:20,471
but I hope people will discover the joy...

1383
01:01:20,472 --> 01:01:22,601
of experiencing new flavours.

1384
01:01:22,602 --> 01:01:24,642
I will take my leave with that in mind.

1385
01:01:26,072 --> 01:01:28,812
The biggest problem with this is that...

1386
01:01:29,282 --> 01:01:31,242
everyone is doing so much better than I expected.

1387
01:01:31,752 --> 01:01:33,722
I learned a lot from them. I really did.

1388
01:01:34,052 --> 01:01:36,522
Everyone says running a business is really hard.

1389
01:01:37,692 --> 01:01:41,122
I need to gain more experience and keep building up,

1390
01:01:41,662 --> 01:01:42,892
without getting complacent.

1391
01:01:43,622 --> 01:01:45,861
I suddenly heard the sound of the shutter...

1392
01:01:45,862 --> 01:01:48,132
coming down behind me with a loud noise.

1393
01:01:49,202 --> 01:01:51,172
I showed everything I wanted to show.

1394
01:01:51,332 --> 01:01:53,942
I feel like I can go home with a light and happy heart.

1395
01:01:55,242 --> 01:01:58,041
Hearing people say things like I'm desperately struggling...

1396
01:01:58,042 --> 01:01:59,271
or trying way too hard...

1397
01:01:59,272 --> 01:02:01,182
actually hurt my feelings at times.

1398
01:02:02,542 --> 01:02:04,222
But I realised one thing while doing this.

1399
01:02:04,652 --> 01:02:07,132
Isn't desperately struggling better than wasting my life away?

1400
01:02:07,822 --> 01:02:08,982
I want to do even better.

1401
01:02:10,952 --> 01:02:13,352
Running a business is way too hard.

1402
01:02:14,292 --> 01:02:17,162
I feel like I know which direction the answer lies in,

1403
01:02:17,362 --> 01:02:19,861
but the path has split into even more branches.

1404
01:02:19,862 --> 01:02:21,231
Now I've gotten many more concerns.

1405
01:02:21,232 --> 01:02:23,272
- We have more concerns now.
- It's more difficult.

1406
01:02:24,032 --> 01:02:26,172
Since we're only in our sixth year,

1407
01:02:26,272 --> 01:02:28,801
I believe we still have many chances to learn and grow.

1408
01:02:28,802 --> 01:02:29,802
That's true.

1409
01:02:30,172 --> 01:02:33,372
Hee Eun! We ended up going home together.

1410
01:02:34,082 --> 01:02:35,082
Let's go.

1411
01:02:35,382 --> 01:02:37,142
Let's go back to Busan and run our business.

1412
01:02:37,912 --> 01:02:39,311
(The sales status of the revival match)

1413
01:02:39,312 --> 01:02:41,121
(1st place: Essence And Technique, 529 dollars)

1414
01:02:41,122 --> 01:02:43,242
(2nd place: Everything About Tteokbokki, 377 dollars)

1415
01:02:49,622 --> 01:02:52,892
(The largest theme park in Korea)

1416
01:02:53,592 --> 01:02:56,732
(An average of 14,000 visitors per day)

1417
01:02:56,832 --> 01:02:58,832
No one goes there just to eat.

1418
01:02:59,032 --> 01:03:01,301
It is better to wait in line and ride one more attraction.

1419
01:03:01,302 --> 01:03:02,918
I thought people in the amusement park...

1420
01:03:02,942 --> 01:03:06,112
would like to try something special.

1421
01:03:06,912 --> 01:03:09,482
Things like churros or tornado potatoes.

1422
01:03:09,842 --> 01:03:12,081
- Food you eat while walking around.
- Food you eat while walking around.

1423
01:03:12,082 --> 01:03:13,588
(Food that is convenient to carry around?)

1424
01:03:13,612 --> 01:03:15,821
Something both children...

1425
01:03:15,822 --> 01:03:17,291
and adults can enjoy.

1426
01:03:17,292 --> 01:03:19,422
(Food that can satisfy multiple target customers?)

1427
01:03:19,522 --> 01:03:22,562
How can we satisfy every target customer at the same time?

1428
01:03:22,822 --> 01:03:25,232
(The Third Street Arena: An amusement park)

1429
01:03:28,262 --> 01:03:29,931
(At 6am, an amusement park in Yongin)

1430
01:03:29,932 --> 01:03:32,771
We now have two teams that came back...

1431
01:03:32,772 --> 01:03:34,272
through the revival match.

1432
01:03:35,442 --> 01:03:38,172
- Who are they?
- I knew it. Who survived?

1433
01:03:38,212 --> 01:03:39,772
I knew this would happen.

1434
01:03:46,912 --> 01:03:48,022
My goodness.

1435
01:03:51,322 --> 01:03:53,792
- They survived!
- Tteokbokki is alive!

1436
01:03:54,862 --> 01:03:57,862
Everything About Tteokbokki was like a phoenix. Impressive.

1437
01:03:58,262 --> 01:04:00,231
As for Everything About Tteokbokki,

1438
01:04:00,232 --> 01:04:03,662
they've finally met the mission that's perfect for them.

1439
01:04:05,432 --> 01:04:09,002
Essence And Technique is a team that is remarkably good at business.

1440
01:04:09,242 --> 01:04:10,372
I'm back.

1441
01:04:10,972 --> 01:04:12,212
You guys better watch out.

1442
01:04:12,972 --> 01:04:15,582
Underdog revival teams often end up winning the whole thing.

1443
01:04:18,482 --> 01:04:22,452
This round is the 100 serving relay team match.

1444
01:04:24,252 --> 01:04:27,022
(Team One: Jung Ho Young and Hong Seok Cheon)

1445
01:04:27,122 --> 01:04:29,562
(Team Two: Edward Kwon and Kim Mi Ryeong)

1446
01:04:29,662 --> 01:04:32,362
(Team Three: Go Seok Hyun and Lee Sung Hoon)

1447
01:04:32,432 --> 01:04:35,202
(Team Four: Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon)

1448
01:04:35,262 --> 01:04:38,372
(Team Five: Lee Yeon Bok and Kim Min Seong)

1449
01:04:38,472 --> 01:04:40,871
(Team Six: Kim Kwan Hoon and Kim Ho Yoon)

1450
01:04:40,872 --> 01:04:44,142
All six alliance teams have now been formed.

1451
01:04:45,472 --> 01:04:46,872
In this round,

1452
01:04:47,282 --> 01:04:49,212
you will operate your restaurants...

1453
01:04:49,582 --> 01:04:51,512
with brand-new signs and interior setups.

1454
01:04:52,152 --> 01:04:53,852
(Wandering Panda)

1455
01:04:54,482 --> 01:04:57,392
(The existing booths will be rotated 90 degrees.)

1456
01:05:00,252 --> 01:05:03,362
This round will be conducted as a blind test.

1457
01:05:04,592 --> 01:05:08,262
One member from each alliance team is allowed to leave the booth...

1458
01:05:08,402 --> 01:05:10,602
while wearing a full-body mascot costume.

1459
01:05:11,602 --> 01:05:15,072
However, you cannot speak a single word.

1460
01:05:16,842 --> 01:05:20,242
We will now reveal the containers you will use to sell your food.

1461
01:05:20,372 --> 01:05:22,682
- Containers?
- What's that?

1462
01:05:22,912 --> 01:05:24,212
- What?
- What are these?

1463
01:05:24,312 --> 01:05:26,381
- What's that?
- What? Are they containers?

1464
01:05:26,382 --> 01:05:28,181
How we utilize these containers...

1465
01:05:28,182 --> 01:05:30,422
will serve as a key strategy.

1466
01:05:30,522 --> 01:05:32,251
Since it’s an amusement park,

1467
01:05:32,252 --> 01:05:34,562
we had to think about convenience.

1468
01:05:34,762 --> 01:05:38,062
So what required a lot of strategic consideration...

1469
01:05:38,132 --> 01:05:39,231
was the container selection.

1470
01:05:39,232 --> 01:05:41,672
I didn't know they would make us choose containers like that.

1471
01:05:41,932 --> 01:05:43,652
(The first container: A soda pop container)

1472
01:05:43,702 --> 01:05:46,572
(The second container: A half-and-half bowl)

1473
01:05:46,632 --> 01:05:49,042
(The third container: A rectangular tray)

1474
01:05:49,372 --> 01:05:51,511
(The fourth container:)

1475
01:05:51,512 --> 01:05:53,542
(A cauldron-shaped bowl)

1476
01:05:54,542 --> 01:05:56,641
(They must choose 2 out of these 4 containers...)

1477
01:05:56,642 --> 01:05:59,912
(and sell 13-dollar menu items.)

1478
01:06:00,052 --> 01:06:03,222
(Beverage included)

1479
01:06:04,952 --> 01:06:07,921
(A 13-dollar combo menu)

1480
01:06:07,922 --> 01:06:09,821
The rectangular tray is for Japanese food.

1481
01:06:09,822 --> 01:06:12,332
It could be for Japanese, Korean, or even gimbap.

1482
01:06:12,792 --> 01:06:14,601
You could put anything in that one.

1483
01:06:14,602 --> 01:06:16,132
Being long wouldn't matter.

1484
01:06:16,332 --> 01:06:18,771
It has to be two distinct food items.

1485
01:06:18,772 --> 01:06:19,831
Since it’s half and half,

1486
01:06:19,832 --> 01:06:21,872
you can let them combine and eat them together.

1487
01:06:22,272 --> 01:06:23,871
Chop steak seems like a good option.

1488
01:06:23,872 --> 01:06:25,372
Anyway, steak has to be included.

1489
01:06:26,042 --> 01:06:27,681
I have no idea what we're supposed to sell in this one.

1490
01:06:27,682 --> 01:06:28,881
- This isn't good.
- It's too difficult.

1491
01:06:28,882 --> 01:06:29,912
- This is bad.
- This...

1492
01:06:30,212 --> 01:06:32,581
This one is quite hard to pull off.

1493
01:06:32,582 --> 01:06:34,863
It will be too tough to compose the menu items with that.

1494
01:06:35,322 --> 01:06:39,391
The teams will sell in relays using two types of containers.

1495
01:06:39,392 --> 01:06:41,168
(They will select two types of containers for their business.)

1496
01:06:41,192 --> 01:06:44,691
The starting team must complete selling out all 50 portions...

1497
01:06:44,692 --> 01:06:46,191
(Sold out)

1498
01:06:46,192 --> 01:06:49,201
before the second team can take over the business.

1499
01:06:49,202 --> 01:06:50,361
(The 1st dish must sell out to unlock the 2nd containers.)

1500
01:06:50,362 --> 01:06:52,532
Only the teams that sell out all 100 servings first,

1501
01:06:52,972 --> 01:06:57,072
including the 2nd team's 50 servings, will survive.

1502
01:06:58,542 --> 01:07:00,242
This will be fun.

1503
01:07:00,342 --> 01:07:01,482
All right, we can do this.

1504
01:07:02,412 --> 01:07:04,682
The number of restaurants to survive in this round...

1505
01:07:06,552 --> 01:07:08,321
is only two.

1506
01:07:08,322 --> 01:07:09,382
What?

1507
01:07:10,082 --> 01:07:12,752
My goodness. This can't be real.

1508
01:07:13,192 --> 01:07:18,992
(Only two alliance teams survive.)

1509
01:07:19,792 --> 01:07:21,562
Only two teams will survive?

1510
01:07:21,932 --> 01:07:25,302
In this round, if customer dissatisfaction occurs,

1511
01:07:26,702 --> 01:07:29,302
a penalty will be applied, adding one more serving...

1512
01:07:29,672 --> 01:07:31,171
from your count.

1513
01:07:31,172 --> 01:07:33,812
(There are 100 containers in total that need to be sold.)

1514
01:07:34,112 --> 01:07:37,142
(If they receive a rating of 2 stars or lower, )

1515
01:07:37,282 --> 01:07:40,512
(1 extra container is added.)

1516
01:07:40,652 --> 01:07:43,952
That means we might have to sell more than 50 servings.

1517
01:07:45,022 --> 01:07:47,142
So a single dish needs to deliver total satisfaction.

1518
01:07:47,722 --> 01:07:49,861
We will have to cook really well.

1519
01:07:49,862 --> 01:07:50,862
Right.

1520
01:07:50,863 --> 01:07:52,862
How many penalties are we going to get?

1521
01:07:53,232 --> 01:07:55,802
Those penalties are going to act as a crucial variable.

1522
01:07:56,362 --> 01:08:00,032
The amusement park opens at 10am.

1523
01:08:00,872 --> 01:08:04,841
Please begin preparing for operations.

1524
01:08:04,842 --> 01:08:08,382
(Remaining time until the opening of restaurants)

1525
01:08:21,822 --> 01:08:23,398
I'm confident when it comes to team battles.

1526
01:08:23,422 --> 01:08:24,492
I really am.

1527
01:08:24,832 --> 01:08:27,962
The goal is for both of us to win after all. I want to win.

1528
01:08:28,202 --> 01:08:30,102
The team we had in mind was...

1529
01:08:31,432 --> 01:08:32,432
The Sauce.

1530
01:08:32,433 --> 01:08:33,732
(The Sauce by Choi Sang Hyun)

1531
01:08:34,202 --> 01:08:35,801
I wanted to do it with someone who knows what they're doing.

1532
01:08:35,802 --> 01:08:37,772
The first restaurant to survive...

1533
01:08:38,212 --> 01:08:40,342
(1st place in Round 1, the 1,000-dollar sales race)

1534
01:08:40,812 --> 01:08:42,782
(A 2-to-0 victory in the 1,000-dollar sales race)

1535
01:08:42,882 --> 01:08:45,052
I've known Chef Sang Hyun of The Sauce...

1536
01:08:45,182 --> 01:08:47,481
for over ten years now.

1537
01:08:47,482 --> 01:08:48,522
Hoon!

1538
01:08:49,122 --> 01:08:50,752
If we teamed up,

1539
01:08:50,892 --> 01:08:52,592
I thought we would have great teamwork.

1540
01:08:52,752 --> 01:08:54,192
HunGry is doing very well.

1541
01:08:54,622 --> 01:08:55,861
I want to be there.

1542
01:08:55,862 --> 01:08:57,092
- Here or there?
- Yes.

1543
01:08:57,562 --> 01:08:58,632
Do whatever you want.

1544
01:08:59,262 --> 01:09:00,361
Can I pick?

1545
01:09:00,362 --> 01:09:01,631
The location doesn't matter.

1546
01:09:01,632 --> 01:09:03,792
- Right. It doesn't matter.
- We just need to do well.

1547
01:09:05,202 --> 01:09:06,902
It felt reassuring.

1548
01:09:07,202 --> 01:09:09,072
With the four of us on a team,

1549
01:09:09,202 --> 01:09:10,802
I thought our individual skill levels...

1550
01:09:10,972 --> 01:09:13,112
were top-tier, to be honest.

1551
01:09:14,242 --> 01:09:16,782
We met up and held about 3 or 4 meetings.

1552
01:09:17,082 --> 01:09:19,751
We need to choose an item with strong appeal.

1553
01:09:19,752 --> 01:09:21,651
Whoever sells out first wins the round.

1554
01:09:21,652 --> 01:09:23,551
People will come solely based on the sign.

1555
01:09:23,552 --> 01:09:26,051
They have no idea who is actually cooking back there.

1556
01:09:26,052 --> 01:09:28,238
First, we need to figure out our primary target customers.

1557
01:09:28,262 --> 01:09:31,062
The people coming between 12pm and 3pm...

1558
01:09:31,592 --> 01:09:33,931
- Right. Mostly preschool kids.
- They are mostly preschoolers.

1559
01:09:33,932 --> 01:09:36,402
And the moms with young kids who aren't in kindergarten.

1560
01:09:36,702 --> 01:09:38,872
Maybe we can name our team...

1561
01:09:39,102 --> 01:09:41,342
something like "Kid-Friendly."

1562
01:09:42,302 --> 01:09:44,141
- The team name isn't important.
- That doesn't matter.

1563
01:09:44,142 --> 01:09:46,241
I think it could work as part of our strategy.

1564
01:09:46,242 --> 01:09:48,458
I love it. I love the idea of the name and kid-friendly dishes.

1565
01:09:48,482 --> 01:09:50,742
- But it doesn't quite sound catchy.
- I know.

1566
01:09:50,912 --> 01:09:53,112
It could rather be something like "Kids' Menu."

1567
01:09:53,682 --> 01:09:55,352
- Kids...
- "Kids Restaurant."

1568
01:09:55,422 --> 01:09:56,622
- Kids Restaurant!
- Yes.

1569
01:09:57,652 --> 01:09:59,621
Let's go with that. Kids Restaurant.

1570
01:09:59,622 --> 01:10:01,102
- Kids Restaurant.
- Kids Restaurant.

1571
01:10:01,422 --> 01:10:03,862
(Kids Restaurant!)

1572
01:10:04,432 --> 01:10:08,032
(Kids Restaurant!)

1573
01:10:09,602 --> 01:10:11,532
(Free cotton candy)

1574
01:10:11,672 --> 01:10:12,802
Aren't you too cute, Hoon?

1575
01:10:12,902 --> 01:10:15,672
Hurry and put it on. We all need to wear it.

1576
01:10:15,742 --> 01:10:17,842
- This is hilarious.
- It's cute.

1577
01:10:19,612 --> 01:10:21,242
We had a reason for this.

1578
01:10:21,612 --> 01:10:23,741
The concept of our booth was "Kids Restaurant."

1579
01:10:23,742 --> 01:10:25,352
I got this hat for the theme.

1580
01:10:26,052 --> 01:10:28,212
It's such a shame the customers won't get to see this.

1581
01:10:29,352 --> 01:10:31,592
- Go, Kids Restaurant!
- Go!

1582
01:10:32,592 --> 01:10:33,852
I don't know.

1583
01:10:34,722 --> 01:10:38,591
Dishes that are hard for toddlers and young kids to eat,

1584
01:10:38,592 --> 01:10:40,662
such as spicy food with strong flavours.

1585
01:10:41,062 --> 01:10:43,562
We ruled out those dishes when coming up with the menu.

1586
01:10:43,832 --> 01:10:46,802
So we prepared a cream pasta specifically targeted at children.

1587
01:10:47,642 --> 01:10:50,241
(Steak cream pasta)

1588
01:10:50,242 --> 01:10:52,112
The operating hours are from 12pm to 3pm,

1589
01:10:52,542 --> 01:10:54,088
so people will want to have lunch from 12pm.

1590
01:10:54,112 --> 01:10:55,812
We allocated more than...

1591
01:10:56,042 --> 01:10:58,752
two-third of our food budget to the first dish.

1592
01:10:59,282 --> 01:11:01,298
So we decided that the starting team would serve...

1593
01:11:01,322 --> 01:11:02,952
a cost-effective and delicious meal.

1594
01:11:03,422 --> 01:11:06,391
If you can get steak and pasta for 13 dollars,

1595
01:11:06,392 --> 01:11:07,521
who wouldn't eat here?

1596
01:11:07,522 --> 01:11:09,862
- I love the idea.
- I think that sounds good.

1597
01:11:09,992 --> 01:11:11,561
Where else could you get steak and pasta for 13 dollars?

1598
01:11:11,562 --> 01:11:12,662
- It's impossible.
- Right.

1599
01:11:12,862 --> 01:11:14,192
For the first race,

1600
01:11:14,432 --> 01:11:17,002
we chose the rectangular tray.

1601
01:11:17,402 --> 01:11:21,272
It is the container that presents the food with the most variety.

1602
01:11:22,572 --> 01:11:23,741
Seung Jae, did you set the water on the stove?

1603
01:11:23,742 --> 01:11:24,912
Yes.

1604
01:11:26,312 --> 01:11:29,242
- Is everything going well, Hoon?
- Yes. I have no problems.

1605
01:11:29,582 --> 01:11:31,582
I felt we needed a leader anyway.

1606
01:11:31,712 --> 01:11:34,552
We entrusted that leadership role to Chef Sang Hyun.

1607
01:11:34,852 --> 01:11:36,251
How long do you think this will take, Hoon?

1608
01:11:36,252 --> 01:11:37,751
- The blending?
- Yes.

1609
01:11:37,752 --> 01:11:38,821
Three more minutes.

1610
01:11:38,822 --> 01:11:41,261
After you do that, measure out...

1611
01:11:41,262 --> 01:11:42,822
- the tomato paste, Jong In.
- Okay.

1612
01:11:43,692 --> 01:11:44,861
Seung Jae, are you keeping an eye on the beef?

1613
01:11:44,862 --> 01:11:45,862
Yes.

1614
01:11:48,532 --> 01:11:51,502
Since I'm older, I spoke comfortably to everyone.

1615
01:11:51,872 --> 01:11:54,272
I organised things well and passed them along.

1616
01:11:54,802 --> 01:11:56,522
Seung Jae, did you hydrate the breadcrumbs?

1617
01:11:57,242 --> 01:11:58,272
Not yet.

1618
01:11:58,512 --> 01:11:59,872
You do that.

1619
01:11:59,972 --> 01:12:01,812
Jong In, put in the chocolate syrup.

1620
01:12:02,182 --> 01:12:04,882
And let's grind some cheese for the garnish.

1621
01:12:06,752 --> 01:12:09,072
Even without lengthy explanations, they understood well...

1622
01:12:09,422 --> 01:12:10,952
and knew what they had to do.

1623
01:12:12,052 --> 01:12:15,392
We took care of our own tasks while blending into the team.

1624
01:12:15,692 --> 01:12:16,991
While the ice cream is freezing,

1625
01:12:16,992 --> 01:12:18,832
- I'll go make cotton candy outside.
- Okay.

1626
01:12:19,292 --> 01:12:22,702
We brought individual timetables for all four of us.

1627
01:12:23,362 --> 01:12:25,032
Having a timeline set up like that...

1628
01:12:25,332 --> 01:12:27,172
ensures our work gets completed on schedule...

1629
01:12:27,402 --> 01:12:29,342
and stays on tempo.

1630
01:12:30,372 --> 01:12:33,041
I don't think any other team prepared as thoroughly as we did.

1631
01:12:33,042 --> 01:12:35,342
We're doing things that require a lot of work.

1632
01:12:35,582 --> 01:12:36,942
- It takes the most effort.
- Yes.

1633
01:12:37,142 --> 01:12:39,951
Compared to teams that were formed in a hurry,

1634
01:12:39,952 --> 01:12:42,082
I think our teamwork was much better.

1635
01:12:42,722 --> 01:12:44,721
I bet we will finish right on time. Let's do this.

1636
01:12:44,722 --> 01:12:45,792
(Kids Restaurant)

1637
01:12:47,292 --> 01:12:48,522
- Hey.
- Yes?

1638
01:12:48,892 --> 01:12:50,662
Do we have any chant?

1639
01:12:50,692 --> 01:12:51,692
- A chant?
- A chant?

1640
01:12:51,693 --> 01:12:53,453
- Chef Land, hey, hey, hey!
- Hey, hey, hey!

1641
01:12:53,962 --> 01:12:57,232
(Jung Ho Young and Hong Seok Cheon)

1642
01:12:57,632 --> 01:12:59,272
Here's my opinion.

1643
01:12:59,632 --> 01:13:01,341
We should sell...

1644
01:13:01,342 --> 01:13:03,942
the drink combo first.

1645
01:13:04,072 --> 01:13:06,071
- Serve that first?
- Yes.

1646
01:13:06,072 --> 01:13:07,371
(Hohyunghojae chose the soda pop container.)

1647
01:13:07,372 --> 01:13:09,541
I noticed in the table layout,

1648
01:13:09,542 --> 01:13:11,182
there weren't that many tables.

1649
01:13:11,312 --> 01:13:13,151
(600 seats in Sejong)

1650
01:13:13,152 --> 01:13:14,981
(400 seats in Songdo with the mat zone)

1651
01:13:14,982 --> 01:13:15,982
(150 seats in the amusement park)

1652
01:13:15,983 --> 01:13:18,183
We chose the one most suitable for the commercial zone.

1653
01:13:18,222 --> 01:13:21,561
People can't help but get a takeout.

1654
01:13:21,562 --> 01:13:24,322
That's why we chose the soda pop container.

1655
01:13:24,662 --> 01:13:28,602
Our strategy is to have you wear the mask in the first half,

1656
01:13:28,732 --> 01:13:30,461
and we'll deal with the sales first.

1657
01:13:30,462 --> 01:13:34,672
We expected people to grab a meal at noon.

1658
01:13:34,842 --> 01:13:39,212
Then people will choose something rather light later.

1659
01:13:39,342 --> 01:13:41,482
The first meal to serve is...

1660
01:13:41,642 --> 01:13:45,112
Korean rib-eye party cup grilled by the chef.

1661
01:13:46,012 --> 01:13:47,982
Let me quickly work on this first.

1662
01:13:48,352 --> 01:13:49,621
Get the meat ready.

1663
01:13:49,622 --> 01:13:51,892
- I'll mature it first.
- Yes, that's important.

1664
01:13:52,222 --> 01:13:54,762
I found high quality Korean beef, right?

1665
01:13:55,262 --> 01:13:56,721
I thought people in the amusement park...

1666
01:13:56,722 --> 01:13:59,931
would like to try something special.

1667
01:13:59,932 --> 01:14:02,132
So we chose Korean beef for our ingredient.

1668
01:14:02,362 --> 01:14:04,332
(In the morning of Round 3)

1669
01:14:04,872 --> 01:14:06,632
Korean beef? Rib-eye?

1670
01:14:07,532 --> 01:14:09,272
- Oh, Korean rib-eye?
- Korean rib-eye?

1671
01:14:11,772 --> 01:14:13,411
How did they meet the price range with rib-eye?

1672
01:14:13,412 --> 01:14:14,442
That's tough.

1673
01:14:14,642 --> 01:14:16,981
They're using Korean beef...

1674
01:14:16,982 --> 01:14:18,662
when it should be around 12 to 13 dollars?

1675
01:14:19,012 --> 01:14:20,751
It's impossible to meet the price.

1676
01:14:20,752 --> 01:14:22,582
Are they able to meet the price?

1677
01:14:22,852 --> 01:14:24,822
I'm curious about the rib-eye.

1678
01:14:25,452 --> 01:14:27,591
Tell me about the manufacturer.

1679
01:14:27,592 --> 01:14:29,298
(All teams are given the same ingredient cost.)

1680
01:14:29,322 --> 01:14:30,462
It's 570 dollars.

1681
01:14:30,922 --> 01:14:33,132
It costs only 270 dollars for 9kg of rib-eye?

1682
01:14:33,392 --> 01:14:34,392
What?

1683
01:14:34,393 --> 01:14:36,002
Can you get Korean beef for that price?

1684
01:14:36,302 --> 01:14:38,772
We'll get frozen...

1685
01:14:38,932 --> 01:14:40,731
- Grade 2 or 3 Korean beef.
- I see.

1686
01:14:40,732 --> 01:14:41,872
Yes.

1687
01:14:42,072 --> 01:14:45,312
We're using frozen Grade Two Korean beef.

1688
01:14:45,912 --> 01:14:48,511
- It'll be just over 480 dollars.
- Around 480 dollars?

1689
01:14:48,512 --> 01:14:49,642
Help us out.

1690
01:14:49,912 --> 01:14:52,411
- Try not to go...
- Over...

1691
01:14:52,412 --> 01:14:53,982
- over high 300 dollars.
- Okay.

1692
01:14:54,152 --> 01:14:56,051
Our budget is low.

1693
01:14:56,052 --> 01:14:58,352
It's the same menu, but made with beef?

1694
01:14:58,722 --> 01:15:00,192
Then I'd totally buy that too.

1695
01:15:00,792 --> 01:15:02,821
Korean beef was our kick.

1696
01:15:02,822 --> 01:15:05,262
But since we had to meet the Korean beef price,

1697
01:15:05,332 --> 01:15:08,431
we as chefs have the technique...

1698
01:15:08,432 --> 01:15:11,432
to tenderize the chewy meat.

1699
01:15:11,932 --> 01:15:14,402
I think this was a very good idea, Seok Cheon.

1700
01:15:14,842 --> 01:15:16,742
To add the stock powder.

1701
01:15:17,342 --> 01:15:19,771
We tenderized the meat...

1702
01:15:19,772 --> 01:15:22,242
by adding the stock powder and baking soda.

1703
01:15:22,812 --> 01:15:25,381
The veggies are pretty good for ugly veggies.

1704
01:15:25,382 --> 01:15:26,512
- Yes.
- Yes.

1705
01:15:26,852 --> 01:15:29,451
- With ugly veggies.
- They're not actually ugly.

1706
01:15:29,452 --> 01:15:30,822
They're just a bit small.

1707
01:15:31,122 --> 01:15:33,922
We used ugly veggies.

1708
01:15:34,052 --> 01:15:37,692
So we can save the ingredient cost and lower the price.

1709
01:15:38,362 --> 01:15:40,231
You're too smart...

1710
01:15:40,232 --> 01:15:41,802
for your skills.

1711
01:15:41,962 --> 01:15:43,902
My nickname is the fat fox.

1712
01:15:44,502 --> 01:15:46,232
A fat fox? Okay.

1713
01:15:47,232 --> 01:15:49,442
- It's 10:10am.
- Okay.

1714
01:15:50,042 --> 01:15:51,371
- It's 10:10am.
- Let's start making...

1715
01:15:51,372 --> 01:15:53,512
- cotton candies at 10:30am.
- Okay.

1716
01:15:56,712 --> 01:16:01,112
(Stir-frying ingredients endlessly)

1717
01:16:06,152 --> 01:16:08,162
- What time is it?
- It's 10:30am.

1718
01:16:08,692 --> 01:16:09,862
- Hoon.
- Yes.

1719
01:16:10,292 --> 01:16:11,592
Can you count the meat for me?

1720
01:16:12,062 --> 01:16:13,332
I lost count while counting.

1721
01:16:13,792 --> 01:16:16,332
Two, four, six, eight, ten.

1722
01:16:16,832 --> 01:16:17,972
Twenty two.

1723
01:16:18,302 --> 01:16:20,202
We won't be able to finish in time.

1724
01:16:20,532 --> 01:16:22,801
- What?
- We won't be ready in time.

1725
01:16:22,802 --> 01:16:23,802
What do we do?

1726
01:16:24,142 --> 01:16:27,142
Actually, it required a lot of ingredients.

1727
01:16:27,312 --> 01:16:29,812
And the sauce was too complicated.

1728
01:16:29,912 --> 01:16:32,011
They pan-fried Korean beef.

1729
01:16:32,012 --> 01:16:33,572
Then they grilled it on charcoal again.

1730
01:16:33,912 --> 01:16:36,952
There was so much to do that the prep time felt short.

1731
01:16:37,252 --> 01:16:39,198
Chef Song Hoon, is there anything else you want me to do?

1732
01:16:39,222 --> 01:16:41,391
Since it's a team match,

1733
01:16:41,392 --> 01:16:43,162
we had to cook like their menu was our own.

1734
01:16:43,292 --> 01:16:45,992
Here's what you need to do. Turn on high heat...

1735
01:16:46,262 --> 01:16:47,532
and cook only the outside.

1736
01:16:48,062 --> 01:16:50,861
(Jung Ho Young's french fries)

1737
01:16:50,862 --> 01:16:53,631
(Jung Ho Young's Korean beef skewer)

1738
01:16:53,632 --> 01:16:56,942
I expected them to need my help.

1739
01:16:57,142 --> 01:16:58,442
It's a small space,

1740
01:16:58,542 --> 01:17:00,372
and I knew what they were making.

1741
01:17:00,642 --> 01:17:02,612
We avoided using a knife as much as possible.

1742
01:17:02,812 --> 01:17:06,151
If we make enough in one large pot...

1743
01:17:06,152 --> 01:17:08,852
and make the sauce on the side,

1744
01:17:08,952 --> 01:17:11,282
it'll be efficient as if we're working as one team.

1745
01:17:11,792 --> 01:17:14,892
Chef Min Hyuk worked very hard.

1746
01:17:15,022 --> 01:17:16,622
He was our cheat code.

1747
01:17:17,222 --> 01:17:20,631
(Team Chef Land's cheat code, Park Min Hyuk)

1748
01:17:20,632 --> 01:17:22,502
He helped them diligently.

1749
01:17:22,732 --> 01:17:25,032
It was not a problem. We're a team after all.

1750
01:17:25,772 --> 01:17:28,742
If we get extra points for teamwork,

1751
01:17:29,142 --> 01:17:30,702
we'd totally make it.

1752
01:17:32,242 --> 01:17:34,142
Cotton candy will go crazy later.

1753
01:17:35,142 --> 01:17:37,382
Are they giving it out for free?

1754
01:17:37,782 --> 01:17:39,182
I think the cotton candy was free.

1755
01:17:39,612 --> 01:17:40,982
They have a good business tactic.

1756
01:17:41,152 --> 01:17:43,982
It'd be funny if only the two of us become popular.

1757
01:17:44,692 --> 01:17:46,592
Kids Restaurant has...

1758
01:17:47,592 --> 01:17:48,662
cotton candy.

1759
01:17:49,822 --> 01:17:51,662
They're serving cotton candy and ice cream.

1760
01:17:53,362 --> 01:17:56,531
Kids Restaurant and we had a similar theme.

1761
01:17:56,532 --> 01:17:59,472
They were serving cotton candy or churros.

1762
01:17:59,602 --> 01:18:03,402
In fact, they even had the ice cream machine ready.

1763
01:18:04,002 --> 01:18:06,411
But then Hoon's cotton candy...

1764
01:18:06,412 --> 01:18:08,942
- looks nice.
- If you shape it like that...

1765
01:18:09,042 --> 01:18:11,241
It depends on how they serve it.

1766
01:18:11,242 --> 01:18:12,812
I bet they can't do it.

1767
01:18:13,082 --> 01:18:16,222
There's a big difference between an owned restaurant and a rent.

1768
01:18:16,452 --> 01:18:18,121
I once had cotton candy in the menu...

1769
01:18:18,122 --> 01:18:21,122
for about three years in the past.

1770
01:18:21,592 --> 01:18:23,322
At first, this is what you do.

1771
01:18:26,562 --> 01:18:27,562
Good job.

1772
01:18:27,563 --> 01:18:29,561
Did you learn that from CIA?

1773
01:18:29,562 --> 01:18:31,032
Not from CIA.

1774
01:18:31,632 --> 01:18:33,232
- It looks like a UFO.
- Yes.

1775
01:18:34,872 --> 01:18:37,902
Our cotton candy is on another level.

1776
01:18:38,172 --> 01:18:40,512
It looks nice, and it has a nice colour.

1777
01:18:40,812 --> 01:18:42,042
Look, Hoon.

1778
01:18:43,182 --> 01:18:44,242
The cotton candy.

1779
01:18:44,982 --> 01:18:46,412
Theirs doesn't have a shape.

1780
01:18:46,552 --> 01:18:47,651
- No?
- Are they making it?

1781
01:18:47,652 --> 01:18:49,522
- It's messy.
- Really?

1782
01:18:49,652 --> 01:18:51,121
They only focused on serving it.

1783
01:18:51,122 --> 01:18:52,798
- They only focused on serving it.
- That's perfect.

1784
01:18:52,822 --> 01:18:56,422
I took a peek at their cotton candy.

1785
01:18:56,792 --> 01:18:58,731
That's not cotton candy.

1786
01:18:58,732 --> 01:19:00,062
That's just cotton.

